> Dear All
>
> I am trying to fit a zero inflated model in INLA using  Prob(y|...) =
> p x 1[y=0] + (1 - p) x Poisson(y | y > 0). Is there a possibility to
> model p as a function of covariates.

yes. since the poisson part is y|y>0, you can. see
