With regards to the prior effect on the range: Your results are what I would expect.
"range parameter seem to vary from 7-20 ... stdev ... 2-5..."
This makes sense! With a lot of data, the data should dominate the (one-dimensional) priors, and a solid change in priors should only somewhat affect the posteriors. This is great!

Haakon

