> > > > > > > > It sounds like you're asking for something that would be relevant for an MCMC run, and not a direct calculation like INLA. That said, the optimization step of INLA is the closest relative of that, and convergence to the mode is checked as part of the termination for the numerical optimization algorithm. The verbose=TRUE option to inla() will show you the optimization, including the residual and gradient values used to determine that a mode has been reached.
